    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a fair distinction, but if you look at the data, the growth metrics for that period are pretty undeniable, right? it feels like trying to argue the policies \"failed\" because of inequality is kind of ignoring the massive boom they created. wouldn't it be more accurate to say the model worked exactly as intended, even if the distribution wasn't perfect?",
